# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/window-next four-card DEVELOPMENT window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/window-next and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the branch. The device pieces of serving_octo.DEVICE_PIECES are BUILT on the host and tested
# on CPU; none of them has run on a card, and the admission logs every card question as an '[OCTO] UNQUALIFIED' line (serving_octo.UNQUALIFIED_ITEMS, each naming the job that settles it).
# Substitute the placeholder in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every
# template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

# Z: the window's end: status and an all-four reset, no agent start (the cards stay under development).
# (window-next: the last job; production is restored by the owner afterwards: card reset, link measurement, topology republish, agent restart, deploy and the post-checks.)

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
